NNAAMMEE
       setarch - change reported architecture in new program environment
       and/or set personality flags

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       sseettaarrcchh [_a_r_c_h] [options] [_p_r_o_g_r_a_m [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t...]]

       sseettaarrcchh ----lliisstt|--hh|--VV

       aarrcchh [options] [_p_r_o_g_r_a_m [_a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t...]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       sseettaarrcchh modifies execution domains and process personality flags.

       The execution domains currently only affects the output of uunnaammee --mm.
       For example, on an AMD64 system, running sseettaarrcchh ii338866 _p_r_o_g_r_a_m will
       cause _p_r_o_g_r_a_m to see i686 instead of _x_8_6___6_4 as the machine type. It can
       also be used to set various personality options. The default _p_r_o_g_r_a_m is
       //bbiinn//sshh.

       Since version 2.33 the _a_r_c_h command line argument is optional and
       sseettaarrcchh may be used to change personality flags (ADDR_LIMIT_*,
       SHORT_INODE, etc) without modification of the execution domain.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       ----lliisstt
           List the architectures that sseettaarrcchh knows about. Whether sseettaarrcchh
           can actually set each of these architectures depends on the running
           kernel.

       ----uunnaammee--22..66
           Causes the _p_r_o_g_r_a_m to see a kernel version number beginning with
           2.6. Turns on UUNNAAMMEE2266.

       --vv, ----vveerrbboossee
           Be verbose.

       --33, ----33ggbb
           Specifies _p_r_o_g_r_a_m should use a maximum of 3GB of address space.
           Supported on x86. Turns on AADDDDRR__LLIIMMIITT__33GGBB.

       ----44ggbb
           This option has no effect. It is retained for backward
           compatibility only, and may be removed in future releases.

       --BB, ----3322bbiitt
           Limit the address space to 32 bits to emulate hardware. Supported
           on ARM and Alpha. Turns on AADDDDRR__LLIIMMIITT__3322BBIITT.

       --FF, ----ffddppiicc--ffuunnccppttrrss
           Treat user-space function pointers to signal handlers as pointers
           to address descriptors. This option has no effect on architectures
           that do not support FFDDPPIICC ELF binaries. In kernel v4.14 support is
           limited to ARM, Blackfin, Fujitsu FR-V, and SuperH CPU
           architectures.

       --II, ----sshhoorrtt--iinnooddee
           Obsolete bug emulation flag. Turns on SSHHOORRTT__IINNOODDEE.

       --LL, ----aaddddrr--ccoommppaatt--llaayyoouutt
           Provide legacy virtual address space layout. Use when the _p_r_o_g_r_a_m
           binary does not have PPTT__GGNNUU__SSTTAACCKK ELF header. Turns on
           AADDDDRR__CCOOMMPPAATT__LLAAYYOOUUTT.

       --RR, ----aaddddrr--nnoo--rraannddoommiizzee
           Disables randomization of the virtual address space. Turns on
           AADDDDRR__NNOO__RRAANNDDOOMMIIZZEE.

       --SS, ----wwhhoollee--sseeccoonnddss
           Obsolete bug emulation flag. Turns on WWHHOOLLEE__SSEECCOONNDDSS.

       --TT, ----ssttiicckkyy--ttiimmeeoouuttss
           This makes sseelleecctt(2), ppsseelleecctt(2), and ppppoollll(2) system calls
           preserve the timeout value instead of modifying it to reflect the
           amount of time not slept when interrupted by a signal handler. Use
           when _p_r_o_g_r_a_m depends on this behavior. For more details see the
           timeout description in sseelleecctt(2) manual page. Turns on
           SSTTIICCKKYY__TTIIMMEEOOUUTTSS.

       --XX, ----rreeaadd--iimmpplliieess--eexxeecc
           If this is set then mmmmaapp(3p) PPRROOTT__RREEAADD will also add the PPRROOTT__EEXXEECC
           bit - as expected by legacy x86 binaries. Notice that the ELF
           loader will automatically set this bit when it encounters a legacy
           binary. Turns on RREEAADD__IIMMPPLLIIEESS__EEXXEECC.

       --ZZ, ----mmmmaapp--ppaaggee--zzeerroo
           SVr4 bug emulation that will set mmmmaapp(3p) page zero as read-only.
           Use when _p_r_o_g_r_a_m depends on this behavior, and the source code is
           not available to be fixed. Turns on MMMMAAPP__PPAAGGEE__ZZEERROO.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

